**What the numbers say.** The synthetic peaks are oversaturated (a share of
[[eval.fixed_time.morning_peak.unfinished_share.mean:.2f]] of the vehicles does not finish within the
hour even under fixed-time, and insertion delays are several minutes), so waiting-time means of
completed trips must be read together with throughput and `mean_depart_delay` in
`results/main_table.csv`. With this CPU budget the safe PPO policy does **not** beat the baselines on
vehicle delay: max-pressure is clearly best on waiting time in every scenario, and PPO lands close to
fixed-time (seed 13 slightly better, seed 42 worse). PPO does cut pedestrian waiting
([[eval.ppo.morning_peak.ped_mean_wait.pct_vs_fixed:pct]] in the morning peak) and the shield never had
to intervene. The contribution of this repository is the safety construction, the mixed-traffic
simulation and the reproducible pipeline, not a performance claim; see `docs/report.md` section 6.

